---
title: "College Composition I"
code: "ENG-111"
category: "english"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

[See Table E for Placement](#Table_E)

Introduces and prepares students to the critical processes and fundamentals of writing in academic and professional contexts. Teaches the use of print and digital technologies to promote inquiry. Requires the production of a variety of academic texts, totaling at least 4500 words (15 pages typed) of polished writing. This course requires proficiency in using word processing and learning management software. This is a Passport Transfer course. Lecture 3 hours per week.
